We need origin_availability_locked and confirmed etc. We'll do load/unload for origin and destination as earlier.

Now we need to ensure we have candidate_prepared for both before load/unload. We have that after steps.

Now we need to ensure we have origin_availability_node_linked and destination_availability_node_linked (they are true from init and not changed).

Now we need to ensure we have not inadvertently locked availability via load (which locks) and we need locked true for goal; we will get that from load actions.

Now we need to ensure we have not accidentally unlocked availability via any action. Unload does not affect locked. Good.

Now we need to ensure we have not accidentally made cargo unavailable at end; after both load+unload sequences, cargo will be available again (since each load consumes cargo, each unload releases). So after origin load+unload, cargo available; after destination load+unload, cargo available again. So final cargo_available true (not required but fine).

Now we need to assemble transport leg: we need origin_availability_locked and destination_availability_locked (true after loads), origin_availability_confirmed and destination_availability_confirmed (true after unloads), origin_node_ready and destination_node_ready (true after activates), transport_leg_available (still true). Also need origin_availability_node_linked and destination_availability_node_linked (true). So we can assemble after both unloads.

Now we need to execute schedule dispatch for shift_candidate_alpha. We have dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha (init), candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma (init), candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha (init). Not dispatched yet. So we can execute execute_schedule_dispatch at any point after those are true (they are from init and not changed). However note that execute_schedule_dispatch will make vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma and dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha. It will not affect other needed predicates. We can do it at the end.

Now we need to ensure we haven't inadvertently changed any of those preconditions: e.g., we might have changed vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_alpha? No. candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma remains true (no action touches it). candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha remains true (no action touches it). dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha remains true (no action touches it). So preconditions hold throughout.

Now we need to verify that we didn't accidentally change candidate_prepared shift_candidate_alpha? Not needed.

Now we need to check that we didn't accidentally change candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha etc. Not needed.

